# ANTI-REGRESSION POSITIVE — C1. Ratified by D10(b) ADDENDUM 3 + its same-day
# amendment (`docs/define-gorget/decisions.md`, end of the LOG).
#
# At an aggregate-init OWNED-FIELD position, a bare read is exempt from the
# place-overlap rule ON THE MOVER AXIS: a move transfers a pointer and cannot
# invalidate a sibling read, so `Pair(v[0], !v)` is sound. All three spellings
# below must ACCEPT, run ASan-clean, and print the PRE-MOVE element value.
#
#   1. struct ctor with an index read      Pair(v[0], !v)
#   2. tuple literal twin                  (w[0], !w)
#   3. get-chain view read                 Pair(u.get(0).unwrap(), !u)
#
# CORRECT TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `--sanitize`): all three
# accept and print their payloads with no sanitizer report. This fixture exists
# so the D10 structural-chokepoint rebuild cannot "fix" the writer-axis holes by
# blanket-rejecting aggregate init — that would ship a new OVER-rejection, which
# is precisely what brief-review pass 1 caught in the Track-A brief v1.
#
# ⚠ ORACLE LANE LAG (ggdef, measured this session): ggdef REJECTS this program —
#   error[E_BorrowConflict]: cannot pass `v` and `!v` in the same call
# ggdef still routes aggregate init through the CALL-shaped check and has not
# yet implemented ADDENDUM 3's mover exemption, which was ratified the same day
# these fixtures were written. So this is a KNOWN, EXPECTED ggdef lag on a
# ratified widening (Core #9), not evidence against the ruling — ggdef must be
# brought to ACCEPT in the round that lands the chokepoint. The intended state
# asserted here is the RULING's, which production already implements.
#
# Contrast:
#   * `sound_excl_nested_writer_ctor.gg` — sibling WRITER, must REJECT.
#   * `sound_ctor_mover_first_reject.gg` — mover FIRST, must reject on the
#     LIVENESS axis (`E_UseAfterMove`), not the aliasing axis.
struct Pair:
    String s
    Vector[String] rest

void main():
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push("alpha-heap-forced-payload")
    Pair p = Pair(v[0], !v)
    print(p.s)

    Vector[String] w = Vector[String]()
    w.push("beta-heap-forced-payload")
    (String, Vector[String]) t = (w[0], !w)
    print(t.0)

    Vector[String] u = Vector[String]()
    u.push("gamma-heap-forced-payload")
    Pair q = Pair(u.get(0).unwrap(), !u)
    print(q.s)
